### Third-Party Earth Observation Data Attribution (ESA Copernicus Sentinel-1 & Sentinel-2)

This software accesses, processes, and displays Earth observation radar and optical data
from the **Copernicus Programme**, operated by the European Space Agency (ESA) and the
European Commission, governed by **Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) No 1159/2013**
establishing a free, full, and open data access policy.

- **Mandatory Attribution**: *"Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data [2026]"*.
- **Sensors Used**:
  - **Sentinel-1 SAR**: C-Band Synthetic Aperture Radar (5.405 GHz) dual-polarization (VV/VH)
    for all-weather cloud-penetrating moisture saturation and canopy structural roughness.
  - **Sentinel-2 MSI**: Multispectral Level-2A surface reflectance (10m/20m) for vegetative
    indices (NDVI, EVI, NDWI) with Scene Classification Layer (SCL) cloud filtering.
- **European Space Agency / Copernicus Dataspace Portal**: https://dataspace.copernicus.eu

---

### Third-Party Agroclimatic & Topographic Attribution (NASA POWER, SRTM & GPM)

This project integrates open agroclimatological, digital elevation, and precipitation products
provided by the **National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA)** under the
**NASA Earth Science Data Policy** (Directives **NPD 2230.1** and **SPD-41A**):

- **NASA POWER Project**: Prediction of Worldwide Energy Resources, NASA Langley Research Center
  (solar radiation, temperature series, humidity, and Growing Degree Days calculation).
- **NASA SRTM & GPM**: Shuttle Radar Topography Mission digital elevation models (30m) and
  Global Precipitation Measurement constellation real-time rainfall data.
- **NASA Earthdata / POWER Portal**: https://power.larc.nasa.gov

